  "content": {
    "id": "p148-intersections-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "For which values of $k$ will the line $y=k$ intersect the following curves twice?",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p148-intersections-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2+y^2=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2<k<2$",
          "worked": "The circle has centre $(0,0)$ and radius $\\sqrt{4}=2$. A horizontal line intersects it twice strictly between its lowest and highest levels. At $k=-2$ and $k=2$, the line is tangent and there is only one intersection.\n\n$$-2<k<2$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p148-intersections-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=9-\\sqrt{4-x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7<k\\le9$.\n\nExclude the minimum level $7$; include $9$, which meets both endpoints.",
          "worked": "This is the lower semicircle with centre $(0,9)$ and radius $2$. Its lowest point is $(0,7)$, so $k=7$ gives only one intersection. Its endpoints are $(-2,9)$ and $(2,9)$, so $k=9$ gives two intersections. Every horizontal level strictly between $7$ and $9$ also gives two intersections.\n\n$$7<k\\le9$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
